description:
QA (qa-b29f7b3d) approved WT-07 (task-b319b263) with one non-blocking gap, recorded in its reviewSummary as "ps1: 3/4 killed. Survivor, non-blocking: control seat routed to the shared path. With no baseline that path also lands nothing here."

The gap is in the wt-control-seats case (WT7D) of scripts/tests/postflight-worktree.cjs. The case still passes when moe-agent.ps1 sends an architect or QA control seat down the shared landing path instead of Invoke-MoeControlSeatPostflight. With no pre-flight baseline, the shared path also lands nothing, so every assertion holds on both routes:
- one nothing/checkpoint/MOE_COMMIT_NOTHING_TO_COMMIT row;
- for-each-ref unchanged;
- HEAD stays on moe/control;
- the control write is kept;
- no baseline is written.
A regression in the control-seat route would therefore go unnoticed.

QA's suggested fix: give the case an ASSERTED path (declare_files) or a TOOL-witnessed path that the shared path would commit.

When this row is promoted, slot it into the wrapper-lane dependsOn chain (pinned #general msg-6c3c0ede).
